should not decorate an outcome that is merely unequal. Descriptive reporting can still guide allocation well when it clearly shows which posts contribute and how much uncertainty remains about future repetition."]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"deep-dive","className":"article-prose deep-dive","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Heavy tails are not a licence to spray"}],[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["A few posts carrying much of a campaign's reach can be an operational fact without proving a particular mathematical distribution. Calling every uneven chart a power law gives the analysis more authority than it earned. Start with the observable concentration: how much of the total came from the largest posts, how many accounts contributed, and how much work sat behind the attempts? This is enough to ask useful budget questions. You do not need a grand theory of the feed to notice that the median attempt and the portfolio total tell different stories."]}]]}]],["$","figure",null,{"className":"editorial-diagram diagram-compare","children":[["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mono acid","children":"THE IDEA, UNPACKED"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Concentration is a starting point"}]]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"diagram-items","children":[["$","li","Observe",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"01"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Observe"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Measure how much a few posts contribute."}],false]}]]}],["$","li","Account",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"02"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Account"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Include the cost of every attempted concept."}],false]}]]}],["$","li","Decide",{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"diagram-index","children":"03"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Decide"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Fund bounded exploration with explicit learning questions."}],false]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"diagram-caption","children":"Editorial model: a way to reason about the process, not measured platform results."}]]}],["$L1e"]]}],false,false,"$L1f","$undefined","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23"]}],"$L24"]}]
1a:["$","section",null,{"className":"related-grid","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":["$","h2",null,{"children":"Other currents."}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-grid","children":[["$","$L25","059",{"a":{"id":"059","author":"jet","slug":"top-ten-accounts","category":"lab","term":"Account concentration","kind":"protocol","image":"top-ten-accounts","media":"$1:props:children:1:props:next:media","en":{"title":"Multi-Account Analytics: Measure Performance Concentration","dek":"Account concentration shows which assets carry the total outcome."},"readingMinutes":2},"lang":"en"}],["$","$L25","057",{"a":{"id":"057","author":"jet","slug":"percentiles","category":"lab","term":"Distribution percentiles","kind":"protocol","image":"percentiles","media":"$1:props:children:1:props:previous:media","en":{"title":"Social Media Analytics: How to Read Performance Percentiles","dek":"A percentile locates a value in an ordered distribution."},"readingMinutes":2},"lang":"en"}],["$","$L25","001",{"a":{"id":"001","author":"organic-club-editorial","slug":"distribution-is-the-moat","category":"doctrine","term":"Account-Generated Distribution","kind":"essay","image":"distribution-is-the-moat","media":{"kind":"illustration","src":"/images/iceberg.jpg","width":1536,"height":1024,"alt":{"en":"Night iceberg with a green submerged mass, a metaphor for unseen distribution."},"credit":"THE ORGANIC CLUB Studio","provenance":"Original AI-generated editorial illustration created for this publication on September 8, 2026. Not a documentary photograph.","source":"https://theorganiclub.com/images/iceberg.jpg","license":"Original artwork","licenseUrl":"https://theorganiclub.com/en/about/#images"},"en":{"title":"What Is AGD Marketing? Account-Generated Distribution Explained","dek":"Everyone can produce. Almost nobody knows how to distribute. Welcome to the other side of the iceberg."},"readingMinutes":5},"lang":"en"}]]}]]}]
1e:["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","$1d","0",{"children":[["$","p","0",{"children":["The tempting response is to publish more of everything. That works only if extra attempts preserve enough creative quality, account stewardship and learning capacity to be useful. Otherwise volume expands the bill while making the data harder to interpret. Allocate a bounded exploration budget, retain unsuccessful attempts in the record, and examine whether new concepts or repeated versions created the upside. A portfolio can justify experimentation. It does not justify assuming that the next thousand weak posts contain an inevitable winner."]}]]}]]}]
